      "explanation": "The factor \\(2000^{2000}\\) is a product of \\(2000\\) copies of \\(2000\\). Multiplying by one more copy gives \\(2001\\) copies. Equivalently, the same-base exponent rule gives\n\\[\n2000(2000^{2000})\n=2000^1\\cdot2000^{2000}\n=2000^{2001}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2000^{2001}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
